  "result": "Perfect! All 174 tests pass. Here's a summary of what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary: Payment Terms Support\n\nI've successfully added payment terms functionality to the invoicing system.\n\n### New Features\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`**\n- `createInvoice()` now accepts an optional `terms` parameter ('NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM')\n- Defaults to 'NET30' if not specified\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on all created invoices\n- Validates terms and returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown values\n- All invoice operations (`addLine`, `removeLine`, `issueInvoice`) preserve terms and due date\n\n**New functions in `src/dates.js`**\n- `lastDayOfMonth(date)`: Calculates the last day of a month (handles leap years)\n- `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`: Calculates due date based on payment terms\n  - 'NET14': 14 days after issue date\n  - 'NET30': 30 days after issue date\n  - 'EOM': Last day of the issue date's month\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Payment terms must be \"NET14\", \"NET30\", or \"EOM\".\"\n\n**Updated `src/payments.js`**\n- `recordPayment()` preserves terms and dueDate when recording payments\n\n### Test Coverage\n\nAdded 12 comprehensive tests to `test/invoices.test.js`:\n- Default NET30 terms\n- NET14 term calculations\n- NET30 term calculations\n- EOM (end-of-month) calculations\n- EOM for different month lengths (31, 30, 28, 29 days)\n- Invalid terms validation\n- Terms preservation through invoice operations (addLine, removeLine, issueInvoice)\n\n**Test Results**: All 174 tests pass (162 existing + 12 new tests for payment terms)",
